{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Docker Scout",
          "informationUri": "https://docker.com/products/docker-scout",
          "name": "docker scout",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107778",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107778"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-107778?s=debian&n=krb5&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "MIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service.\n\n---\n- krb5 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/pull/1511\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/48afa9abb89ab2176bb20624d87d010b9984fc08 (master)\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/62196e2b269159a5465f5b8d0ed7cf6f29c3282a (krb5-1.22 branch)\n",
                "markdown": "> MIT Kerberos 5 (krb5) through 1.22.2 contains a NULL pointer dereference in make_cred_list() in rd_cred.c that allows authenticated Kerberos clients to crash services by sending mismatched KRB-CRED arrays. Attackers can send forwarded credentials with more tickets than ticket_info entries through gss_accept_sec_context() to crash GSS-API acceptor services, causing denial of service.\n\n---\n- krb5 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/krb5/krb5/pull/1511\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/48afa9abb89ab2176bb20624d87d010b9984fc08 (master)\nFixed by: https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/62196e2b269159a5465f5b8d0ed7cf6f29c3282a (krb5-1.22 branch)\n\n|                                                                                                      |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/krb5@1.21.3-5%2Bdeb13u1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                    |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                             |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/krb5@1.21.3-5%2Bdeb13u1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-107161",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-107161"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-107161?s=debian&n=cyrus-sasl2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in Cyrus SASL. The add_to_challenge() function in the DIGEST-MD5 plugin computes the size of the buffer needed for a challenge/response field before DIGEST-MD5 quoting is applied, but does not recompute that size when quoting (escaping special characters) makes the value longer. The under-sized buffer is then passed to strcat(), causing a heap-based out-of-bounds write whose size depends on attacker-controlled input. A malicious or on-path DIGEST-MD5 (or HTTP Digest) server can trigger this flaw in a connecting client by supplying a crafted challenge field, such as realm or nonce, most likely resulting in a crash of the client application.\n\n---\n- cyrus-sasl2 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/cyrusimap/cyrus-sasl/issues/889\nhttps://github.com/cyrusimap/cyrus-sasl/pull/892\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2460420\n",
                "markdown": "> A heap-based buffer overflow flaw was found in Cyrus SASL. The add_to_challenge() function in the DIGEST-MD5 plugin computes the size of the buffer needed for a challenge/response field before DIGEST-MD5 quoting is applied, but does not recompute that size when quoting (escaping special characters) makes the value longer. The under-sized buffer is then passed to strcat(), causing a heap-based out-of-bounds write whose size depends on attacker-controlled input. A malicious or on-path DIGEST-MD5 (or HTTP Digest) server can trigger this flaw in a connecting client by supplying a crafted challenge field, such as realm or nonce, most likely resulting in a crash of the client application.\n\n---\n- cyrus-sasl2 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/cyrusimap/cyrus-sasl/issues/889\nhttps://github.com/cyrusimap/cyrus-sasl/pull/892\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2460420\n\n|                                                                                                           |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/cyrus-sasl2@2.1.28%2Bdfsg1-9?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                         |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/cyrus-sasl2@2.1.28%2Bdfsg1-9?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-67693",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-67693"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-67693?s=debian&n=gnutls28&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "An issue in gnutls v.3.8.13 allows an attacker to obtain sensitive information via failing to reject end-entity X.509 certificates that contain a contradictory combination of Key Usage (KU) and Extended Key Usage (EKU)\n\n---\n- gnutls28 <unfixed>\nTODO: check if https://gist.github.com/lkloliver/6fbfc191bc6163942c8017551ac3f238 reported upstream, valid?\n",
                "markdown": "> An issue in gnutls v.3.8.13 allows an attacker to obtain sensitive information via failing to reject end-entity X.509 certificates that contain a contradictory combination of Key Usage (KU) and Extended Key Usage (EKU)\n\n---\n- gnutls28 <unfixed>\nTODO: check if https://gist.github.com/lkloliver/6fbfc191bc6163942c8017551ac3f238 reported upstream, valid?\n\n|                                                                                                         |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/gnutls28@3.8.9-3%2Bdeb13u4?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                       |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                |\n"
