            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-77214",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-77214"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-77214?s=debian&n=expat&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "libexpat before commit 13c5f63 contains a heap buffer over-read vulnerability in xmlparse.c. XML_ParseBuffer advances the parse buffer end with parser->m_bufferEnd += len using a caller-supplied length that is not validated against the allocated buffer size, so repeated XML_ParseBuffer calls move m_bufferEnd past the end of the heap allocation and subsequent parsing reads out of bounds. Reaching this path requires a parse buffer to already be present; otherwise XML_ParseBuffer returns XML_ERROR_NO_BUFFER. A buffer is present after a prior call to XML_GetBuffer, either directly (the common case) or indirectly through a prior XML_Parse call that allocates the buffer internally. The over-read discloses adjacent heap memory to the calling application, recovering heap pointers, libc function pointers, and code pointers sufficient to defeat ASLR and build further exploitation primitives.\n\n---\n- expat 2.9.0-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1150320)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1393\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/4d9b1c499ecb66323260a7274edcf86c5eab0517 (R_2_9_0)\n",
                "markdown": "> libexpat before commit 13c5f63 contains a heap buffer over-read vulnerability in xmlparse.c. XML_ParseBuffer advances the parse buffer end with parser->m_bufferEnd += len using a caller-supplied length that is not validated against the allocated buffer size, so repeated XML_ParseBuffer calls move m_bufferEnd past the end of the heap allocation and subsequent parsing reads out of bounds. Reaching this path requires a parse buffer to already be present; otherwise XML_ParseBuffer returns XML_ERROR_NO_BUFFER. A buffer is present after a prior call to XML_GetBuffer, either directly (the common case) or indirectly through a prior XML_Parse call that allocates the buffer internally. The over-read discloses adjacent heap memory to the calling application, recovering heap pointers, libc function pointers, and code pointers sufficient to defeat ASLR and build further exploitation primitives.\n\n---\n- expat 2.9.0-1 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1150320)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1393\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/4d9b1c499ecb66323260a7274edcf86c5eab0517 (R_2_9_0)\n\n|                                                                                                    |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/expat@2.8.3-1~deb13u1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                  |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                           |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/expat@2.8.3-1~deb13u1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.3",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-85091"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-85091?s=debian&n=zlib&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary.\n\n---\n- zlib <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146895)\nhttps://gist.github.com/thesmartshadow/e0b9481792afb7c31e86fee1ff084490\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/issues/1310\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/pull/1317\nFixed by: https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/df84af25dc1942490e1d1c899a07619152a46148\nDiscussion on affected range: https://github.com/madler/zlib/issues/1310#issuecomment-5979623265\nSupport non-blocking devices in the gz* routines introduced with:\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/81cc0bebedd935daeb81b0b6e475d8786b51af3d (v1.3.1.2)\n",
                "markdown": "> zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary.\n\n---\n- zlib <unfixed> (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1146895)\nhttps://gist.github.com/thesmartshadow/e0b9481792afb7c31e86fee1ff084490\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/issues/1310\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/pull/1317\nFixed by: https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/df84af25dc1942490e1d1c899a07619152a46148\nDiscussion on affected range: https://github.com/madler/zlib/issues/1310#issuecomment-5979623265\nSupport non-blocking devices in the gz* routines introduced with:\nhttps://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/81cc0bebedd935daeb81b0b6e475d8786b51af3d (v1.3.1.2)\n\n|                                                                                                                |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/zlib@1%3A1.3.dfsg%2Breally1.3.1-1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                              |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/zlib@1%3A1.3.dfsg%2Breally1.3.1-1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.3",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-74860",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-74860"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-74860?s=debian&n=libxml2&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libxml2 with Python bindings enabled. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by providing a specially crafted XML document containing a Document Type Definition (DTD) with enumerated attribute values. This triggers a double-free error in the SAX attributeDecl callback handler, where a string is freed twice. This flaw can lead to a denial of service (DoS) due to a reproducible crash in Python applications using the libxml2 SAX bindings.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.3+dfsg-1\n[bookworm] - libxml2 <postponed> (Minor issue)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2529697\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/work_items/1076\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/merge_requests/397\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f41e1865781f74d1cadfe2fbdfeefed946026f12 (v2.15.3)\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libxml2 with Python bindings enabled. A remote attacker could exploit this vulnerability by providing a specially crafted XML document containing a Document Type Definition (DTD) with enumerated attribute values. This triggers a double-free error in the SAX attributeDecl callback handler, where a string is freed twice. This flaw can lead to a denial of service (DoS) due to a reproducible crash in Python applications using the libxml2 SAX bindings.\n\n---\n- libxml2 2.15.3+dfsg-1\n[bookworm] - libxml2 <postponed> (Minor issue)\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2529697\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/work_items/1076\nhttps://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/merge_requests/397\nFixed by: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libxml2/-/commit/f41e1865781f74d1cadfe2fbdfeefed946026f12 (v2.15.3)\n\n|                                                                                                                                 |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.12.7%2Bdfsg%2Breally2.9.14-2.1%2Bdeb13u3?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                                               |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                                                        |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
                "fixed_version": "not fixed",
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libxml2@2.12.7%2Bdfsg%2Breally2.9.14-2.1%2Bdeb13u3?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.5",
                "tags": [
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-93990",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-93990"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-93990?s=debian&n=expat&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "Expat before 2.8.5 fails to validate that a high surrogate in UTF-16 input is followed by a low surrogate, allowing malformed UTF-16 sequences to be accepted. Attackers can supply UTF-16 encoded XML containing lone high surrogates that consume the following code unit, causing Expat to pass unpaired surrogates to applications built with XML_UNICODE and to silently replace input characters in other builds.\n\n---\n- expat 2.8.4-2 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1148665)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1282\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/0cfd15bdf4b2c22d6b0df73610709dfb60921091 (R_2_8_5)\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/28fcfba540f6933aa8904a1514c4811713d2ab72 (R_2_8_5)\n",
                "markdown": "> Expat before 2.8.5 fails to validate that a high surrogate in UTF-16 input is followed by a low surrogate, allowing malformed UTF-16 sequences to be accepted. Attackers can supply UTF-16 encoded XML containing lone high surrogates that consume the following code unit, causing Expat to pass unpaired surrogates to applications built with XML_UNICODE and to silently replace input characters in other builds.\n\n---\n- expat 2.8.4-2 (bug https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1148665)\nhttps://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/pull/1282\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/0cfd15bdf4b2c22d6b0df73610709dfb60921091 (R_2_8_5)\nFixed by: https://github.com/libexpat/libexpat/commit/28fcfba540f6933aa8904a1514c4811713d2ab72 (R_2_8_5)\n\n|                                                                                                    |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/expat@2.8.3-1~deb13u1?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                  |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                           |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">0",
                "cvssV3_severity": "HIGH",
